<article class="env-remark" id="05B6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05B6">Remark <span data-tag="05B6">35.14.6</span>.</a> With the assumptions (1) and $p$ smooth in Lemma <a href="/tag/05B5" data-tag="05B5">35.14.5</a> it is not automatically the case that $X \to Y$ is smooth. A counter example is $S = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k)$, $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[s])$, $Y = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[t])$ and $f$ given by $t \mapsto s^2$. But see also Lemma <a href="/tag/05B7" data-tag="05B7">35.14.7</a> for some information on the structure of $f$. </p>
</article>